  "mechanismSummary": "A ring π bond attacks the carbon of the acylium ion as a C≡O π bond moves onto oxygen. AlCl₄⁻ removes the proton to give acetophenone. The ketone is less reactive than benzene, so (unlike alkylation) the reaction stops after one acylation; the ketone binds AlCl₃, so a full equivalent is used and released by the aqueous work-up.",
